cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this ontology in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "FRAM Ontology: An OWL 2 Vocabulary for the Functional Resonance Analysis
  Method"
abstract: >-
  An OWL 2 ontology for the Functional Resonance Analysis Method (FRAM),
  enabling formal representation of FRAM models as Linked Data. The ontology
  defines 54 classes and 123 properties (63 object + 60 datatype), 7 SHACL
  shapes, and a JSON-LD context, with a foundational alignment to gUFO (15
  rdfs:subClassOf axioms). This artefact is a research product of the doctoral
  research of César Augusto Simões Goudouris at the Programa de Pós-Graduação
  em Informática (PPGI), Universidade Federal do Rio de Janeiro (UFRJ),
  supervised by Prof. Paulo Victor Rodrigues de Carvalho, DSc (PPGI/UFRJ) and
  Prof. Alessandro Jatobá, DSc (CEE/Fiocruz). Distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0.
